@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Final-only controller validation
+
+Defines the implementation design, work plan and verification ledger for the human-requested CP-004 feature.
+
+## Contract and design
+
+The controller executes its frozen ordered validation profile once, after every milestone has completed implementation and inspection review. No baseline or milestone command runs are permitted. Milestone receipts bind source and inspection evidence with no validation results; only final review receives test results. Every configured command executes at most once, including across interruptions and resume. Final review can inspect failed checks but cannot accept them. Final repair/stop ends the run without further implementation or testing; a new request is needed to repair the source. This strict interpretation preserves the human's once-per-run requirement.
+
+Agents write and inspect tests but never execute tests, reproductions, project imports, or arbitrary code. Disable Codex command execution and other execution-capable tools, and supply a controller-owned read-only source MCP with bounded list/read/search operations. Writer edits remain available through the native patch tool. Do not rely on a test-command blacklist: interpreters, aliases and project wrappers can bypass one. Unsupported required runtime configuration fails closed.
+
+No compatibility migration is required. Advance the snapshot/audit schema to reject old runs under this new lifecycle; retain their original backend and immutable evidence. Preserve Git isolation, role model selections, source binding, leases, quarantine, command supervision, meaningful executed-test evidence, review scope and final receipt/integration gates. No research-product development or live provider calls are part of this task.
+
+## Approaches
+
+- Prompt-only restrictions leave actual controller scheduling and agent execution unchanged and cannot satisfy deterministic enforcement.
+- Command blacklists cannot safely identify arbitrary project test entry points or interpreter use.
+- Selected: change the lifecycle and evidence contracts, remove shell execution from agents, and restore source inspection through a narrow read-only tool surface.
+
+## Implementation plan
+
+### Task 1: Agent execution boundary
+
+- [ ] Add read/list/search MCP protocol regressions for bounded output, traversal, symlink escape, reserved paths, invalid methods/arguments, and subprocess-free behavior.
+- [ ] Implement the dependency-free source MCP and disable command/interpreter/browser execution tools on every Codex invocation, including resume and correction.
+- [ ] Preserve native patch editing and document the replacement inspection tools in common role policy.
+- [ ] Controller runs focused runtime/tool tests; a read-only reviewer inspects the changes without executing tests.
+
+### Task 2: Final-only lifecycle and evidence
+
+- [ ] Add regressions counting commands across multiple milestones, repairs, final review, failure and resume; assert no intermediate Reviewer receives validation evidence.
+- [ ] Remove baseline execution and intermediate validation phases. Bind milestone inspection to exact source with empty validation evidence; reject fabricated milestone check evidence.
+- [ ] Retain one supervised final profile and source-bound final review. Stop final repair without new tests; persist interruption/no-replay guarantees.
+- [ ] Align receipts, criterion evidence, state invariants, loading, diagnostics and schema revision with the lifecycle.
+- [ ] Controller runs focused suites and migrates obsolete scheduling tests to meaningful final-stage coverage.
+
+### Task 3: Prompts, documentation and adoption
+
+- [ ] Update every role/correction policy and current documentation to prohibit agent test execution and describe the final-only lifecycle.
+- [ ] Run the complete deterministic backend suite and runtime configuration probes; report live-test limitations.
+- [ ] Obtain an independent read-only complete-diff review, fix material findings, and verify the final source.
+- [ ] Commit the backend feature, preserve a reviewable patch, adopt the tested commit by exact fast-forward, and update only external feature audit Markdown/indexes.
+
+## Review focus
+
+- Resume after a completed or uncertain validation command must never replay it.
+- Milestone acceptance must not claim tests passed or substitute empty checks for final validation.
+- Failed/skipped-only/stale final evidence must never produce acceptance or merge.
+- Agent inspection must remain useful without a shell, while exposing no arbitrary execution tool.
+- Historical snapshots must be refused rather than silently acquiring the new lifecycle.
+
+## Ledger
+
+- Base: bcb7ad24f83ff5193345f3d4fa72122ea53a4e66; clean original backend and parent. Host inspection found no active controller/role/validator; latest retained status/diagnose confirmed no lease/quarantine/in-flight work. Historical stopped intents remain untouched.
+- Isolation: coding_pipeline/.maintenance/CP-004, branch maintenance/final-only-validation. All task scratch stays under coding_pipeline/.maintenance/.
+- Authority: explicit human implementation request in this conversation, limited to coding_pipeline and external feature logging. No other parent records change.
